  3. Results: paired vs unpaired design
======================================================================

out of 16139 with nonzero total read count
adjusted p-value < 0.05
LFC > 0 (up)       : 2190, 14%
LFC < 0 (down)     : 1891, 12%
outliers [1]       : 0, 0%
low counts [2]     : 313, 1.9%
(mean count < 10)
[1] see 'cooksCutoff' argument of ?results
[2] see 'independentFiltering' argument of ?results

Significant at FDR 5%:  paired design = 4081   unpaired design = 2773 
 Modelling donor removes donor-to-donor variation from the residual noise,
 so the same data gives more power. Ignoring structure = wasting samples.

Columns of the results table:
[1] "mean of normalized counts for all samples"     
[2] "log2 fold change (MLE): dex treated vs control"
[3] "standard error: dex treated vs control"        
[4] "Wald statistic: dex treated vs control"        
[5] "Wald test p-value: dex treated vs control"     
[6] "BH adjusted p-values"                          

